WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.103
Where did the virus

00:00:01.103 --> 00:00:02.780
that changed the world come from?

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:04.740
For a long time, the prevailing theory was

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.870
that wild animals like
bats sold at a wet market

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.400
in Wuhan, China had started the outbreak.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.190
One of the first scientists to question

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.450
this narrative was Botao
Xiao, who on February 6th,

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.700
distributed a paper arguing
that the killer coronavirus

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.970
probably originated from
a laboratory in Wuhan.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.170
The author pointed out
that there was no evidence

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.390
that the vendors at the wet
market in Wuhan sold bat meat.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.740
On the other hand, there
were two research labs

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.160
studying bat-born
coronaviruses located in Wuhan

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.700
where a virus could have
accidentally infected workers

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.900
causing them to spread the
disease to the general public.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.660
Botao Xiao withdrew the
paper two weeks later

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.370
after Chinese authorities declared

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.410
that the lab leak theory had no merit.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.720
China is being accused

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.370
of censoring critical data
about the coronavirus.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.550
The renowned law professor

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.610
at Tsinghua University in
Beijing Xu Zhangrun, is known

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.070
to be missing after publicly condemning

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.160
Chinese president Xi Jinping for failing

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.990
to contain the spread of
the virus at an early stage.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.420
The Chinese government proceeded

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.230
to clamp down on research
into the virus's origins.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.410
New regulations
restricting the publication

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.360
of research about coronavirus.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.190
Any paper that traces the origin

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.240
of the virus should be strictly managed.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.870
To this day, the Chinese
government won't allow

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.320
outside researchers to test blood drawn

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.330
from employees of the Wuhan lab,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.470
who may have been among
the first humans infected

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.210
with COVID in November of 2019.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.950
According to the official record,

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.390
they were hospitalized with
pneumonia-like disease.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.360
There's no proof that the
virus originated from a lab,

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.150
but there's also no proof that
humans first became infected

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.580
by eating bat or exposure to pangolin,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.240
a theory that was treated
as unimpeachable fact

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.550
early in the pandemic.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.210
A group of scientists
signed a statement published

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.300
in The Lancet denouncing speculation

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.660
about non-natural origins of the virus

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.780
as conspiracy theories.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.220
Only after some emails became
public id it become clear

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.000
that the scientists who
brought his colleagues together

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.070
to co-sign The Lancet statement was

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:06.020
Peter Daszak, head of
the EcoHealth Alliance,

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.010
the nonprofit that secured
US government funding

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.330
for controversial research
on bat-born coronaviruses

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.332
at the Wuhan Institute of Virology.

00:02:14.332 --> 00:02:17.830
Daszak also coauthored a June 2020 op-ed

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.663
in The Guardian headlined,

00:02:18.663 --> 00:02:19.496
Ignore the conspiracy theories:

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.770
scientists know COVID-19
wasn't created in the lab,

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.700
without disclosing a potential
conflict of interest.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.680
Media coverage following the publication

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.380
of The Lancet letter
overwhelmingly framed discussion

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.570
of the lab leak hypothesis
as conspiracy theory.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:39.750
That episode does not
reflect well on science.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.540
Science writer Matt Ridley says

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.220
that Anthony Fauci's private
emails, which were made public

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.150
through a Freedom of
Information Act request,

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.790
show that behind the scenes scientists

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.630
were taking the lab leak
theory seriously all along.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.300
A number of leading
virologists were talking

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.527
to each other and we're
saying to each other,

00:02:55.527 --> 00:02:58.930
we think this might
look a bit like a virus

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.200
that's been engineered in a laboratory.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.160
And then they all got on a
phone call with Anthony Fauci,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.290
and at the end of that phone call,

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.290
they all did a very rapid about-face

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.080
and started writing
articles almost immediately.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.880
And in the case of Peter Daszak,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.460
the fact that he had
orchestrated the letter was not

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.020
at all clear until emails were leaked.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.360
It does raise very serious concerns

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.260
that Dr. Daszak needs to answer.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.090
I've tried to correspond
with him numerous times.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:30.310
I've never yet had a response.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.490
Daszak also didn't reply to
Reason's interview request.

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:35.080
Ridley has co-authored "Viral,"

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.810
a new book about the ongoing hunt

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.830
for the origins of the coronavirus.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.470
His writing partner is
Broad Institute of MIT

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.370
and Harvard scientist Alina Chan,

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.230
one of the earliest and most
outspoken public skeptics

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.320
of the natural origin hypothesis.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.340
She says that when she and her colleagues

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.830
published a pre-print
questioning the consensus

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.990
that she hadn't been aware

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.610
of The Lancet letter organized by Daszak,

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.420
but that she believes it
could have had a major

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.630
chilling effect on the
scientific discussion

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.990
in those early days.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.067
So they're saying that anyone who's saying

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.510
that this virus didn't come from

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.230
nature is a conspiracy theorist.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.787
People, when they read this
letter, they might have thought,

00:04:08.787 --> 00:04:10.467
then I'm not going to
put my neck out there

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.390
to say that this might
have come from a lab.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.190
Chan, a molecular biologist,

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.450
argued in the paper that because

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.000
SARS-CoV-2 was so well adapted to humans,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.370
there was reason to be skeptical

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.130
that it had recently come from an animal.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.540
If it had recently come
from bats or pangolins,

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.840
she would have expected the virus

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.940
to have been rapidly
mutating in the early days

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.313
of the pandemic to become
better adapted to human tissue.

00:04:30.313 --> 00:04:33.150
For the, the light bulb moment was when

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:38.090
I read in the news that the
novel coronavirus SARS-CoV-2,

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.710
a pure genetically stable.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.420
Chan credits this insight partially

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:45.110
to her experience living through
the SARS outbreak of 2003,

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.200
which she lived through in Singapore.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.050
In that situation, in that outbreak,

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.750
the virus had rapidly picked
up dozens of mutations

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.840
in the early three months of the outbreak.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.000
In comparison for SARS-CoV-2,

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.750
there are very few of these mutations.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.980
So it suggested to me that this
virus had already picked up

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.410
many useful mutations for infecting

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.240
and transmitting amongst humans prior

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.320
to its detection in December 2019.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.950
Another major difference is that

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.670
during the 2003 outbreak,
authorities discovered

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.560
previous SARS infections
among animals being sold

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.500
at markets in South China
within a couple of months.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.500
That's not the case with SARS-CoV-2,

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.150
despite initial suspicions

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.020
that a seafood market was to blame.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.270
In the case of SARS-2,

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:28.090
even though the first
class of cases identified

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.220
was at the seafood market,

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.650
they never found any signs of animals

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.010
that were infected by this virus.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:37.120
So up till today, there's
no sign of an animal

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.083
that was ever infected by SARS-CoV-2

00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:41.010
and then gave it to humans.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.250
When the World Health
Organization sent a team

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:46.870
to investigate the viruses
origins in January 2021,

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.856
EcoHealth Alliances Daszak was the only

00:05:48.856 --> 00:05:50.750
American member included.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.030
The team dismissed the lab leak hypothesis

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:55.940
before WHO leadership later backtracked.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:59.990
The findings suggest
the laboratory incidents

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.640
hypothesis is extremely unlikely

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:08.660
and to explain the introduction

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.410
of the virus into the human population.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:16.410
And therefore, is not an
hypothesis that we suggest

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.760
that implies to suggest future studies.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.080
Daszak granted an interview

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.370
to 60 Minutes following that trip to Wuhan

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.140
and suggested that farm animals
were the likely culprit.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.030
But there's no direct evidence that any

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:36.190
of those animals were actually
infected with the bat virus.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:37.023
Correct.

00:06:37.023 --> 00:06:39.290
Now what we've got to
do is go to those farms

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.990
and investigate, talk to the farmers,

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:43.230
talk to their relatives, test them,

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.080
see if there were spikes
in virus there first.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.970
So the team doesn't actually know if any

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.140
of the farmers or the
truckers were ever infected.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:53.980
No one knows yet.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.540
No one's been there, no one's asked them,

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:56.520
no one's tested them.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.490
That's to be done.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.760
There's a detail that emerged

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.490
after the "60 Minutes" report that

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.730
Ridley would like Daszak to explain.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.380
Recently leaked documents show that

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.270
EcoHealth Alliance applied
for a research grant related

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:10.000
to inserting what's called
a furin cleavage site

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.602
into SARS-like coronaviruses.

00:07:11.602 --> 00:07:14.940
This very furin cleavage
site make SARS-CoV-2

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:16.600
highly infectious in humans

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.750
and it's what distinguishes it from any

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.970
SARS-like coronaviruses
yet found in the wild.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.770
The grant request was rejected,

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.300
but did the Wuhan laboratory
engage in this research

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.600
even without funding from that grant?

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:31.000
Daszak may be able to help
to answer that question.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.490
The fact that that is probably the feature

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.880
that makes the virus
sufficiently infectious

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.310
to start a pandemic means that

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.083
it is a highly important thing.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:46.240
So you would think that
a scientist who knew

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:51.490
that he had put in a
grant application in 2018

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:56.740
to put furin cleavage site
into SARS-like viruses

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.570
and admittedly been turned down

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:04.740
at the Wuhan Institute of
Virology would volunteer

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:08.160
that information early in the pandemic

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.480
so as to help us understand this new virus

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.330
and understand where
it might've come from.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:15.720
Ridley and Chan also find it suspicious

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.470
that when China's premier
bat coronavirus expert

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.350
and Daszak's collaborator
in Wuhan published

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:24.050
her complete analysis of
the SARS-CoV-2 genome,

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.800
she neglected to mention
this highly unusual

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:29.970
furin cleavage site, but
Daszak told "60 Minutes"

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:33.200
that the WHO did look
into the lab leak theory.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.300
You're just taking their word for it.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.520
Well, what else can we do?

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.880
There's a limit to what you can do

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:39.440
and we went right up to that limit.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.120
We asked them tough questions.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.000
They weren't vetted in advance.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.230
And the answers they gave we found

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:50.000
to be believable, correct, and convincing.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.000
But weren't the Chinese
engaged in a coverup?

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.880
They destroyed evidence.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.150
They punished scientists who were trying

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:00.500
to give evidence on this
very question of the origin.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.760
Well, that wasn't our task to find out

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:04.310
if China had covered up.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.620
It was the behavior of someone

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.870
who is trying to ensure
that one message got out

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:13.110
and not another, which is
fine if you're a politician

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.940
or some kind of opinionated person

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:20.160
and scientists should be
allowed their own opinion.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.900
But it's not fine if you
are being asked to be part

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:28.840
of an objective
international investigation

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:30.460
with privileged access.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.010
After the "60 Minutes" interview,

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.550
leaked documents showed that
EcoHealth Alliance worked

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.560
with the Wuhan Institute of Virology

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:39.610
to make several bat-born
SARS-like coronaviruses,

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.570
and even MERS more
infectious to human cells.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:45.170
Chan and Ridley say that when
they started writing the book,

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.360
they didn't have a strong view

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.860
about which theory was correct.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:51.110
But these recent revelations
have shifted their thinking in

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.347
favor of the lab leak theory.

00:09:53.347 --> 00:09:56.010
In light of grant proposals
and reports released

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.317
within the past few months,
Chan wrote on Twitter,

00:09:58.317 --> 00:10:01.187
we know novel SARS-like
viruses were being synthesized

00:10:01.187 --> 00:10:04.250
and engineered at unprecedented scale.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:05.900
That changed my mind completely.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.580
So knowing that there actually was a plan,

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:13.050
a pipeline, a protocol for
doing this work in 2018.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.450
So now for me, genetic
engineering is very much

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.283
on the table.

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:19.750
It's not just a one out of 10,000 chance

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.070
that this might have happened if it came

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:24.379
from a lab close to 50 percent
chance that it happened.

00:10:24.379 --> 00:10:25.881
This question was at the center

00:10:25.881 --> 00:10:28.880
of a heated exchange between Anthony Fauci

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.010
and Senator Rand Paul
over possible NIH funding

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.280
of so-called gain of function research,

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.290
which involves purposely making a virus

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:37.397
more infectious to humans.

00:10:37.397 --> 00:10:38.900
You take an animal virus

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.310
and you increase the
transferability to humans,

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:42.860
you're saying that's not gain of function?

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:43.693
That is correct.

00:10:43.693 --> 00:10:46.190
And, Senator Paul, you do not know

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:48.510
what you are talking about quite frankly.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.750
And I want to say that officially.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.580
There will be responsibility for those

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:54.672
who funded the lab, including yourself.

00:10:54.672 --> 00:10:55.845
I totally resent-

00:10:55.845 --> 00:10:58.608
This committee will allow
the witness to respond.

00:10:58.608 --> 00:11:00.520
I totally resent the lie

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:03.420
that you are now propagating, Senator.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:06.930
Because if you look at the viruses

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.920
that were used in the experiments

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:13.410
that were given in the annual reports

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.730
that were published in the literature,

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.540
it is molecularly impossible.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.570
No one's saying those viruses caused it.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.770
It is molecularly-
No one is alleging

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.680
those virus cause the pandemic.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.470
What we're alleging is that
gain of function research

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.090
was going on in that
lab and NIH funded it.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.780
You can't get away from it.

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:34.040
It meets your definition and
you are obfuscating the truth.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.240
But much of the blame
for the devastating scope

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.760
of the pandemic, says Ridley,
rests on Chinese authorities

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.280
who punished ophthalmologists Li Wenliang

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:43.590
who tried to get the word out

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.390
about the emergence of
a new SARS-like virus.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.060
The government successfully
kept human to human transmission

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.950
of the disease under wraps
for weeks, maybe longer.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:56.460
Why was such an angst and secrecy

00:11:56.460 --> 00:12:00.550
even at the hyper-local level
from the very beginning?

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:03.110
Communist regimes tend to be secretive.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:06.170
There tends to be an
assumption that you don't talk

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:08.680
about things unless you're allowed to,

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.230
rather than the other way round.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.890
But Xi Jinping is a much more dictatorial

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:16.740
and authoritarian ruler than
his immediate predecessors.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:21.200
And by 2019, it was more and more the case

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.650
that scientists in laboratories

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:27.630
and doctors in hospitals
were under orders not

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:29.680
to communicate with the outside world

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.470
about things that the regime
might not want them to.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.240
Very significant attempts to punish

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:38.240
and suppress the release of information

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.540
about the epidemic that
was developing in Wuhan.

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:44.170
Did that play a part in
the epidemic escaping

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:46.210
and getting to the rest of the world

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:47.950
and turning into a pandemic?

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.040
You bet it did.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.770
If on the 27th, 28th of December,

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.190
when alarm bells were beginning

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.950
to ring in hospitals in Wuhan,

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:57.787
the Chinese authorities
should have said to the world,

00:12:57.787 --> 00:12:59.320
we've got a problem in Wuhan.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.830
We're going to do our best to stop it.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.140
Then we probably could've
pinched this in the bud

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.900
before it got out of the city of Wuhan.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.370
The Wuhan Institute of
Virology houses samples

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:11.310
of RaTG13, a bat virus that is one

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.320
of the closest known genetic
matches to SARS-CoV-2.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.836
But to this day, information
about other coronaviruses

00:13:16.836 --> 00:13:19.750
in the Wuhan lab haven't been released

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.400
so we don't know if the lab
was working with a virus

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.240
that's even more closely
related to SARS-CoV-2.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.590
The lab's public database of viral samples

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:30.280
could hold some answers,
but it was taken offline

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.850
in February and had been
modified in December,

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.720
which we know because of work by DRASTIC,

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:36.930
the Dedicated Research

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.860
and Scientific Team
Investigating COVID-19,

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.750
a decentralized group of volunteers

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.500
that compile and analyze
open-source material

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:48.500
and leaked documents to
investigate the origins of COVID.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.540
They are the heroes of our book.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:55.990
Once I realized that
it's being completely,

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:58.330
it's being discredited
without any evidence,

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.390
I just couldn't stay silent.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.580
Yuri Deigin is a biotech entrepreneur

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.860
and one of the founding
members of DRASTIC.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.480
There was just a group
of like-minded people

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:09.140
on Twitter who got into like
really huge long threads

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.760
on Twitter on some things like

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:14.460
where's the Mojiang
mine or what is RaTG13.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.610
And then at some point, we just
went off to a private group,

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:18.260
which was called Daszak Fan Club,

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:19.860
because pretty much all of us were blocked

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:22.650
by Peter Daszak at some point.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:24.710
A key revelation
uncovered by the group was

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.220
that the Wuhan Institute
of Virology database

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:30.210
was first taken down in September 2019,

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:32.510
three months before the
pandemic became public.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.550
A description of the database was modified

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.900
on December 30th, 2019, the day Dr. Shi

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.800
told Chinese state
television that her lab first

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:44.383
obtained the samples
of the virus In Wuhan.

00:14:57.514 --> 00:15:00.870
Wuhan scientists access
the database a few times

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.490
before it was permanently removed

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:05.830
in February 2020 for
alleged security concerns.

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:07.830
For them to take it down,
it's very suspicious.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:08.873
And of course Shi Zhengli's explanation

00:15:08.873 --> 00:15:11.300
that she took it down to prevent hackers

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.450
from attacking it is complete bullshit

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.550
because it was a public
database to begin with

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:17.220
and what's she afraid of?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:19.500
A member of the DRASTIC
team also discovered

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.210
that the Wuhan team had
collected key samples,

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:25.870
including one of the virus's
closest known genetic matches

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:28.350
from a mine where some
workers had fallen sick

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:30.930
and died after clearing out bat droppings.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.200
Chinese authorities have denied outsiders

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.180
any access to examine the mine.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:39.330
All of these revelations just
reinforced our realization

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.040
that either they're not
telling the truth at all,

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.080
or they're not telling the
whole truth to the world.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.680
And you know, that was a big moment for us

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.200
to kind of start digging
deeper and deeper.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.230
Though there's mounting
circumstantial evidence

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.870
to support the lab leak theory,

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:54.710
most government officials still maintain

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:57.630
that the natural origin
hypothesis is more likely.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.820
A US intelligence report declassified

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:04.190
on October 29th said four Intel
agencies had low confidence

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.020
that the virus most
likely emerged in nature,

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.800
one agency had moderate confidence
that it leaked from a lab

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.160
and analysts at three
agencies remained unable

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.990
to coalesce around either explanation

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.720
without additional information.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.910
The report did conclude
that SARS-CoV-2 was unlikely

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.620
to be a biological weapon.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.650
NIH Director Francis Collins,

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.550
who didn't reply to our interview request,

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:28.450
told computer scientist and
podcast host Lex Fridman

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:31.600
in early November that he's
open to the lab leak hypothesis,

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:32.830
but still believes strongly

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.150
that the virus is of natural origin.

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:36.063
Is there a reasonable chance

00:16:36.063 --> 00:16:39.840
that COVID-19 leaked from a lab?

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.580
I can't exclude that.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.790
I think it's fairly unlikely.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:45.557
I wish we had more ability to be able

00:16:45.557 --> 00:16:48.660
to ask questions of the Chinese government

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:52.160
and learn more about what kind
of records might have been

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:55.230
in the lab that we've
never been able to see.

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:59.180
But most likely, this was a
natural origin of a virus,

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:00.470
probably starting in a bat,

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:02.880
perhaps traveling through
some other intermediate

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:06.620
yet to be identified host and
finding its way into humans.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:09.920
Between July 2020 and January 2021,

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.580
an international team of
scientists captured bats

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.860
in Laos carrying a newly
discovered coronavirus

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:19.270
that's the closest known
genetic match to SARS-CoV-2,

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.810
even closer than the virus
held in the Wuhan lab,

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.670
which some say supports
the natural origin theory.

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.690
But Ridley, Chan, and Deigin point out

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.530
that it lacks the crucial
furin cleavage site,

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:32.340
which they suspect was inserted in a lab.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.960
Supporters of the natural
origin theory point out

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.910
that no smoking gun
virus has yet been found

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.030
in the version of the Wuhan
database uncovered by DRASTIC.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.740
But Chan points out that this version

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.930
of the database is years out of date

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:47.820
because the Wuhan researchers
generally don't enter

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.380
new viruses until they've
had a chance to sequence

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.939
and publish studies about them.

00:17:51.939 --> 00:17:54.020
The Wuhan Institute of Virology

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:55.900
database is still inaccessible.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:59.320
We only see viruses they've
collected up to 2016.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:02.275
So we have barely any
concept of what viruses

00:18:02.275 --> 00:18:04.200
and sequences they might have found

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:07.620
after 2016 in the years
leading up to COVID-19.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.330
So without access to the information

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:13.340
becomes very difficult for us to guess

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.890
whether or not they have
found the precursor of SARS-2

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:17.870
in their labs and were working with it.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:21.140
Of course, also we'd
love to get that database

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:23.168
or at least part of the
data from the database

00:18:23.168 --> 00:18:24.870
that's been deleted and to see

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.990
all the unpublished sequences.

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:29.520
I definitely don't want
to stop biotechnology.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.630
I think CRISPR gene
editing is a fantastic tool

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:36.190
for medicine, for
agriculture, for conservation,

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:37.416
for all sorts of things.

00:18:37.416 --> 00:18:40.900
The overwhelming majority of work

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:43.180
in this field has benefited mankind,

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:46.690
including the development of
the messenger RNA vaccines

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:49.270
that have saved millions
of lives in the last year.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.630
But Ridley says that
scientists should come together

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:54.390
to set ethical guidelines
that prohibit dangerous types

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.510
of research such as experimenting

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.470
on bat viruses to make
them more infectious

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.590
to human cells in large urban environments

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.640
after harvesting them from caves far away

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.700
from human population centers as this

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.560
China-produced documentary
shows researchers doing,

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:11.227
some of them without
proper protective gear.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:32.330
Going out and harvesting
viruses in wild places

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:36.480
and with pandemic potential
and bringing them back

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:41.120
to cities to work on them
probably isn't very sensible.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.400
It's like looking for a gas leak

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.520
with a lighted match as somebody put it.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:50.520
So if we could get the US,
the UK, Australia, Japan,

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:54.427
other major countries
to sign a treaty saying,

00:19:54.427 --> 00:19:56.990
when there's an outbreak in our country,

00:19:56.990 --> 00:20:00.010
we promise to open up as far as possible

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.140
and tell you everything we know,

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:04.161
then the very fact that
some countries won't sign

00:20:04.161 --> 00:20:07.270
that treaty will itself
put pressure on them.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.400
That's kind of the way

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:13.260
the International Atomic
Energy Authority evolved.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:17.320
And I think that's what we
should be looking to achieve.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.340
How optimistic or pessimistic are you

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:24.290
that we ever will get to the
truth of the matter here?

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.610
I'm generally optimistic.

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:27.790
I think truth will out here.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:29.990
It may take a long time.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:33.910
I noticed that the fall of
the Soviet Union did lead

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.830
to significant revelations about

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:39.070
biological accidents there,
for example, anthrax.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:40.940
I think, therefore, it may take a change

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:44.110
of regime in Beijing
before we find out more.

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:47.540
But I think there are people
who know what happened,

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:49.430
whatever had happened, even if it's just

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:53.340
what happened in a market,
there are people who know.

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:56.740
And I can't help thinking
that at some point

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.460
we will be able to find out who they are

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:01.300
and ask even in a regime

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:06.090
as repressive and controlling as China's.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.980
So I hope we do find out.

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:10.420
There are many people
who say it's too late,

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:12.833
we've lost the chance,
we'll never find out.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:15.933
I'm not one of them, at least not yet.

